#X obj 674 8 sequencer;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 286 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A basic sequence player: iterates over a list of elements
and outputs one element per tick. Values can be numbers \, symbols
or nested lists (for example \, "play lists" like (60 127)) \, and
the timing between elements is set by @t. Playback can be looped with
@r \, reversed with @mode \, subdivided with @div and delayed with
@upbeat.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 209 • Melodic sequences — playing a list of notes in order
(for example \, [mtof]-converted pitch values) \, with a fixed interval
between them \, to produce a repeating melodic pattern.;
#X text 250 279 • Simple automation — driving parameter changes in
a repeating pattern \, for example cycling through a list of filter
cutoff values or effect wet/dry levels over time.;
